+## Schedule an Email
+
+Pass `scheduledAt` to `client.messages.send()` to send the message later. Use an ISO 8601 timestamp string or a `Date`.
+
+**Prerequisites:** the SDK is installed and `ACME_MAIL_API_KEY` is set. See the [quickstart](/quickstart).
+
+```js JavaScript
+import { AcmeMail } from '@acme/mail';
+
+const client = new AcmeMail(process.env.ACME_MAIL_API_KEY);
+
+const { messageId, status } = await client.messages.send({
+  from: 'you@example.com',
+  to: 'friend@example.com',
+  subject: 'Your weekly summary',
+  text: 'Here is what happened this week.',
+  scheduledAt: new Date(Date.now() + 60 * 60 * 1000),
+});
+```
+
+A successful call returns a `messageId` and a `status` of `scheduled`. Store the `messageId` if you might cancel the message.
+
+<Note>
+`scheduledAt` must be at least 1 minute and at most 72 hours from now. The SDK throws an error before sending if the time is outside that window or is not a valid date.
+</Note>
+
+## Cancel a Scheduled Email
+
+Call `client.messages.cancel()` with the `messageId` that `send()` returned for a message sent with `scheduledAt`.
+
+**Prerequisites:** the SDK is installed and `ACME_MAIL_API_KEY` is set. See the [quickstart](/quickstart).
+
+```js JavaScript
+import { AcmeMail, AcmeMailError } from '@acme/mail';
+
+const client = new AcmeMail(process.env.ACME_MAIL_API_KEY);
+
+const { messageId } = await client.messages.send({
+  from: 'you@example.com',
+  to: 'friend@example.com',
+  subject: 'Your weekly summary',
+  text: 'Here is what happened this week.',
+  scheduledAt: new Date(Date.now() + 60 * 60 * 1000),
+});
+
+try {
+  const result = await client.messages.cancel(messageId);
+  console.log(result.status);
+} catch (error) {
+  if (error instanceof AcmeMailError && error.code === 'already_sent') {
+    console.error('The send time has passed. The message can no longer be canceled.');
+  }
+}
+```
+
+A successful call returns the `messageId` and a `status` of `canceled`.
+
+<Warning>
+You cannot cancel a message after its send time passes. The call throws an `AcmeMailError` with `status` 409 and `code` `already_sent`.
+</Warning>
+{/* VERIFY: The API returns HTTP 409 with code `already_sent` when `cancel()` is called after the scheduled send time. */}
+
 ## Handle Errors
 
 Failed requests throw an `AcmeMailError` with the HTTP `status` and an API error `code`.
